# The match seed. One integer, or the word `random`.
#
# Everything random in the match descends from it through the named streams in
# src/029-random-streams.lua, so the same seed and the same commands produce the same
# match, tick for tick, on this machine.
#
# `random` draws a fresh one each run and writes it to the append-only notebook at
# tmp/shared-memory/seeds.log, so a match worth keeping can be got back afterwards by
# copying its seed in here. A seed named on the command line -- HLM_SEED -- beats both
# and is not logged, because a seed you typed is one you already have.
random
